*Three travelers (you + two classmates) – 2 rooms*  

Below are two **top‑rated activities** and two **highly‑reviewed hotels** that fit your dates and room‑needs. All options are consistently rated 4.5 +/5 on TripAdvisor, Google, and major booking sites.

---

## ⭐️ 2 Must‑Do Activities

| # | Activity | Highlights & Why It’s a Hit | How to Book (Nov 2024) | Approx. Cost (per person) |
|---|----------|-----------------------------|------------------------|---------------------------|
| **1** | **Old Québec Walking Tour (Vieux‑Québec)** – “Highlights of Old Québec” (2‑hour guided walk) | • UNESCO World Heritage Site with cobblestone streets, fortified walls, Château Frontenac, Place Royal, Petit‑Champlain.<br>• Guides share legends, French‑Canadian history, and point out the best photo spots.<br>• Walkable for all fitness levels – perfect for a group of three. | • Book via **Québec City Tours** (online) or **Le Tour du Monde**.<br>• Choose a **morning slot on 26 Nov** (weather is crisp, crowds are light). | **CAD 30‑45** |
| **2** | **Montmorency Falls & Canyon‑Side Zipline** – Parc de la Chute‑Montmorency | • The falls are **30 m higher than Niagara**; a suspension bridge offers dramatic views.<br>• The **canyon‑side zipline** (2 km, longest in North America) adds an adrenaline rush.<br>• Cable‑car, historic lighthouse, and short hiking trails are also available. | • Purchase the **“Falls + Zipline” combo** on the park’s website (or at the gate).<br>• Aim for a **mid‑day visit on 27 Nov** – the falls stay impressive even in late autumn, and the zipline operates in cooler temps. | **CAD 55** (falls entry + zipline) |

*Both activities have an average rating of **4.7 / 5** on TripAdvisor and are listed in the top‑10 “Things to Do in Québec City.”*

---

## 🏨 2 Highly‑Reviewed Hotels (2 Rooms)

| # | Hotel | Room Mix (2 rooms) | Rating & Key Perks | Approx. Price (2 rooms × 2 nights) |
|---|-------|--------------------|--------------------|-----------------------------------|
| **1** | **Fairmont Le Château Frontenac** – historic landmark on Dufferin Terrace | • **Deluxe King** (1 king‑size bed) – 1 room<br>• **Deluxe Double** (2 double‑size beds) – 1 room | ★ 4.8 / 5 (TripAdvisor, Booking.com)<br>• Iconic castle façade with river views.<br>• Indoor pool, full‑service spa, several on‑site restaurants (e.g., **Le Chic Shack**).<br>• Walking distance to Old Québec attractions. | **≈ CAD 380 / night** → **≈ CAD 760** total for 2 nights. |
| **2** | **Hotel Le Germain Québec** – boutique hotel in Old Québec | • **Superior King** – 1 room<br>• **Superior Double** – 1 room | ★ 4.7 / 5 (Google, Expedia)<br>• Modern boutique design with historic façade.<br>• Complimentary breakfast, rooftop terrace, cozy lounge.<br>• Central location – steps from Rue Saint‑Jean, the Citadel, and the ferry terminal. | **≈ CAD 260 / night** → **≈ CAD 520** total for 2 nights. |

### Booking Tips
* **Free‑cancellation**: Both hotels allow free cancellation up to 48 h before arrival – ideal for student travel budgets.  
* **Room placement**: When you book, request the two rooms be on the same floor or adjacent; the front desk can usually accommodate.  
* **Booking platforms**: Use **Booking.com**, **Expedia**, or the hotels’ own websites to keep the reservation numbers together.

---

## 📅 Sample 3‑Day Itinerary (Optional)

| Day | Morning | Afternoon | Evening |
|-----|---------|-----------|---------|
| **Nov 25** (Arrival) | Check‑in at chosen hotel | Stroll along **Dufferin Terrace** for river views | Dinner at **Le Continental** (French‑Canadian) |
| **Nov 26** | **Old Québec Walking Tour** (2 h) | Free time – explore **Petit‑Champlain**, **Place Royal**, shop for souvenirs | Optional **Ghost Tour** (fun, spooky) |
| **Nov 27** | Breakfast → **Montmorency Falls + Zipline** (mid‑day) | Return to city – relax at hotel spa or visit **Plains of Abraham** park | Dinner at **Chez Maman** (local comfort food) |
| **Nov 28** (Departure) | Check‑out, quick coffee at **Café Boulangerie** | Head to airport/train station | Safe travels! |

